          "parts": [
            {
              "text": "When resolving parenting arrangements and child custody disputes in **Brisbane East and the Bayside (specifically around Carindale, Wynnum, and Manly)**, you have several reputable family law firms and accredited Family Dispute Resolution Practitioners (FDRPs) to consider.\n\nUnder the *Family Law Act 1975*, parents are generally required to make a genuine effort to resolve parenting disputes through an accredited **Family Dispute Resolution (FDR)** process before applying to court for parenting orders (unless an exception such as family violence or urgency applies). \n\n---\n\n### 1. Leading Family Lawyers in the Bayside & Brisbane East\n\n* **Australian Family Lawyers (AFL) – Manly / Bayside**\n  * **Location:** Manly (directly bordering Wynnum).\n  * **Strengths:** AFL is a national firm with a dedicated local Bayside presence. They focus exclusively on family law, with significant experience in parenting plans, complex custody disputes, relocation cases, and representing clients in legally assisted mediations.\n  * **Best For:** Parents who want specialized family litigation experience combined with strong negotiation and mediation representation.\n\n* **Connor Hunter Lawyers – Wynnum**\n  * **Location:** Wynnum (and Cleveland).\n  * **Strengths:** Established in the Bayside area since 1971, Connor Hunter is one of the most rooted firms in Wynnum. They have an established family law team that assists with child custody, parenting agreements, and resolving disputes cooperatively.\n  * **Best For:** Wynnum locals seeking a firm with long-standing ties to the community and experience in local dispute resolution.\n\n* **Daykin Family Law – Serving Carindale & Brisbane East**\n  * **Location:** Brisbane East / Inner East (servicing Carindale and surrounds).\n  * **Strengths:** Led by Shannon Daykin, an Accredited Family Law Specialist and mediator. Daykin Family Law prioritizes keeping parenting disputes out of court where possible through structured negotiations and mediation, but also handles litigated custody hearings.\n  * **Best For:** Carindale residents seeking an accredited specialist approach that emphasizes out-of-court child-focused resolution.\n\n* **Sarah Cleeland Family Lawyers – Bayside / Cleveland**\n  * **Location:** Cleveland (serving the wider Redlands and Bayside corridor).\n  * **Strengths:** A well-regarded boutique family firm known specifically for its dedicated **Parenting Mediation Packages** and **Child-Inclusive Family Dispute Resolution Conferences**. They co-lead sessions with accredited FDRPs and qualified child development experts (such as psychologists or social workers) to bring the child's perspective into the agreement safely.\n  * **Best For:** Complex parenting disputes where parents want an accredited, child-inclusive FDR process without going to court.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Accredited Family Dispute Resolution (Mediation) & Section 60I Certificates\n\nIf you are looking specifically for an **independent accredited mediator (FDRP)** rather than legal representation, remember that an FDRP must remain neutral and cannot give individual legal advice. They are, however, registered to issue a **Section 60I Certificate** if mediation fails or is deemed unsuitable:\n\n* **Bayside Community Legal Service (BCLS) – Wynnum Community Centre**\n  * **Services:** Offers a community-based dispute resolution service with a panel of qualified private mediators and accredited FDRPs. \n  * **Key Advantage:** Free or low-cost services for eligible local residents; panel FDRPs are authorized to issue Section 60I certificates for court if necessary.\n* **Private FDRPs & Parenting Coordinators:**\n  * Independent practitioners such as **Dr. Anne Purcell (Resolution Partners)** or **Jacki Leech (Family Law Mediation)** operate across Brisbane and take referrals for private, fast-tracked parenting mediation and child-focused dispute resolution.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Tips for Choosing the Right Pathway\n\n1. **Clarify the Role You Need:**\n   * If you need someone to **represent and advise you**, hire a family lawyer who can attend mediation with you or negotiate on your behalf.\n   * If you and your former partner both agree to attempt mediation together, engage an **independent accredited FDRP** jointly.\n2. **Consider \"Child-Inclusive\" Mediation:**\n   * If your children are old enough to express views, or if there are disputes over schooling, neurodiverse needs, or living arrangements, firms that offer child-inclusive FDR (where a child consultant meets the child separately) often produce longer-lasting arrangements.\n3. **Turn Agreed Terms into Consent Orders:**\n   * Any agreement reached at mediation (whether via a Parenting Plan or heads of agreement) should be reviewed by a local family lawyer to be drafted into **Consent Orders** filed with the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia, giving the parenting arrangements legal enforceability.",
